  annotation "note_1771582421464_1", anchor: "the specificity I have learned to distrust", text: "Three shamans walked in carrying the Tooth. Three. The pressure-songs name them individually; the names correspond to distinct pressure-signatures in the deep ice. But three is the sacred count in Wake-Singer sacrificial liturgy — offerings in triads. I distrust the number because it is theologically perfect, and because the alternative is that something in the convergence wanted exactly three and stopped accepting volunteers.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582421464_2", anchor: "nine-day circuits beneath the Berg", text: "Nine is the sacred interval in Wake-Singer pressure-liturgy: nine breaths before descent, nine offerings before a major rite. The thermal record shows regular surges but does not resolve to a specific count. The number is likely theological, not observational.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771582421464_3", anchor: "seized control of the site from Wake-Singer remnants during the Orca Incursion without presenting sealed authority", text: "The Guild's jurisdictional claim rests on the Foedus∴vincu — a founding pact that leaves no impression in the deep ice. I noted in my annotation on the Guild that this pact was either sealed somewhere the ice cannot reach or does not exist. The Corpse Current sits in open water. Precisely where the ice cannot reach. This is the first time that observation has troubled rather than amused me.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582421464_4", anchor: "reaching places no orca has ever swum", text: "The Ofundis∴flux breach at Sleek☽ Caemomot produced iron-tasting water in tunnels that have never been connected to the sea. The Nightshelf sealed those tunnels without recording why, which is how they record things that frightened them. Whatever the Current is, it moves through ice. It has been moving through ice longer than anyone has been measuring. The entry describes a location. The margins must hold what it cannot: this is not a place. It is a process.", type: :commentary, display: :full
